  "summary": "Reported: Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3) says the whole office lost internet and nobody on the floor can work. Triage: P1, network_vpn. Checked: her account is active, not blocked, VPN access true, no failed logins. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online=true with a recent check-in and no warnings, so the laptop itself is reachable and the problem looks like the office network/ISP rather than one device. Per KB-014, an office network outage affecting several people is an escalation case. Not yet done: no office-wide network status, switch/firewall/ISP status, or confirmation of how many staff are affected. Needs Tier 2 to check office network core, internet uplink, and any outage on the floor.",
  "reason": "P1 office-wide internet outage affecting multiple staff; KB-014 escalation criteria met. Laptop is online, so the fault is at the network level, beyond Tier 1 tools."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Thanks for reporting this, Priya. I've checked your laptop and it is online and connected to our systems, so the problem looks like it's at the office network level rather than on your machine. I've escalated this to our Tier 2 network team as a priority. They'll check the office network and internet connection. Please let us know if anyone on the floor sees a different problem or if the outage goes away on its own.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user for priya.nair (user_id 3): active, not blocked, no failed logins, VPN access true, device BL-LT-0103. check_device_status on BL-LT-0103: online=true, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:48 UTC, no warnings, disk 62.5% free. Per KB-014, the laptop is reachable, so this is not a single-device fault. The office network is down for several people, which is the KB-014 escalation case. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation_id 1) as P1 with a summary. Not yet verified: office switch/firewall/ISP status and the number of affected staff. No printer checks were run since the report is about internet, not printing.",
